   "text": "This SMILES is my best reading of the drawing. The stereochemistry is the least certain part: I worked out the sugar centres from the wedges and hashes, but for most residues I assumed the natural L configuration rather than confirming it from the drawing.\n\n**Sugar end.** A 1,6-anhydro bicyclic acetal carries NHAc at C2 and OH groups at C3 and C4. The quaternary C5 carries a CH2\u2013O linker, which gives CH2\u2013(OCH2CH2)\u2084 before the triazole. Stereo tags for C1\u2013C5 were derived from the wedges and hashes shown.\n\n**Linker.** The chain runs as follows:\n- A 1,4-disubstituted triazole.\n- CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2.\n- (OCH2CH2)\u2084.\n- C(=O)\u2013NH.\n\n**Lysine.** The linker amide is followed by four CH2 groups to Lys C\u03b1, which is C-terminal CONH2. Its N\u03b1 is acylated by Gly.\n\n**Macrocycle.** Gly leads to Cys, whose sulfur forms a thioether with CH2C(=O). Reading from that thioacetyl N-terminus, the ring is Phe\u2013Val\u2013Pro\u2013Thr\u2013Thr\u2013Bip\u2013N-MeAla\u2013Bip\u2013N-MeAla\u2013Glu\u2013Ala\u2013Pro, closing back onto the Cys nitrogen. Bip is 4-biphenylalanine and Glu has a free CO2H.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H]1[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@]2(COCCOCCOCCOCCn3cc(COCCNC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]4CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccccc5)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(cc5)-c5ccccc5)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(cc5)-c5ccccc5)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5C(=O)N4)nn3)CO[C@H]1O2"
